
##  `read_commit_log`

- loops over git log output
- updates $last_commit_info, and finishes processing on the beginning
  of the next record or at the end of the loop
- the work on $commit_info could effectively happen in the ^= processing
  as all other branches end with a `next` (so the processing is weirdly
  split in two)

## `_make_name_author_info`

- reads from $commit_info, and only the author/commit fields
  to canonicalize
- writes the _canon lines info $commit_info


## Conclusion

rather than having a list of co-authors in the $commit_info hash,
it might be easier to duplicate the $commit_info, once per co-author
and repeat the stats update processing for each of them.

